    <!-- Add static exercises -->

    <exercises>
        <exercise xml:id="PRECALC-7F86FA23T2" original="PRECALC/modules/m49455/index.cnxml" license="CC-BY-4.0">
            <statement>
                <p>Find the average rate of change connecting the points <m>(-5,1.5)</m> and <m>(-2.5,9).</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <answer>
                <p>3</p>
            </answer>
        </exercise>     

        <exercise xml:id="PRECALC-wWwvbN2t0s-parts" original="PRECALC/modules/m49455/index.cnxml" license="CC-BY-4.0">
          <statement>
            <p> For the following pairs of points, find the average rate of change: </p>
            <ol marker="(a)" cols="2">
              <li>
                <m>(-2,0)</m> and <m>(-4,5)</m>
              </li>
              <li>
                <m>(4,-3)</m> and <m>(-2,-1)</m>
              </li>
              <li>
                <m>(0,5)</m> and <m>(6,5)</m>
              </li>
              <li>
                <m>(7,-2)</m> and <m>(7,10)</m>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </statement>
          <solution>
            <ol marker="(a)" cols="2">
              <li>
                <m>-\frac{5}{2}</m>
                </li>
              <li>
                <m>-\frac{1}{3}</m>
              </li>
              <li>
                <m>0</m>
                </li>
              <li>undefined</li>
            </ol>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    
        <exercise xml:id="PRECALC-Iv1ayoeSJv-parts" original="PRECALC/modules/m49455/index.cnxml" license="CC-BY-4.0">
          <statement>
            <p>The revenue generated by selling <m>x</m> items is given by <md>R(x)=2x^{2}+10x</md> Find the average change of the revenue function as <m>x</m> changes from <m>x=10</m> to <m>x=20.</m></p>
          </statement>
          <solution>
            <p>
                We have <m>h = 20 - 10 = 10</m>, so <md>
                    <mrow>\text{ AROC } \amp = \frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} </mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp = \frac{R(20)-R(10)}{10} </mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp = \frac{2(20)^{2}+10(20) - (2(10)^{2}+10(10))}{10} </mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp = \frac{1000 - 300}{10} </mrow>
                    <mrow>\amp = 70 </mrow>
                </md>
            </p>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="PRECALC-XflkuqGf9k-parts" original="PRECALC/modules/m49455/index.cnxml" license="CC-BY-4.0">
          <statement>
            <p>
                The cost of producing <m>x</m> cellphones is described by the function <md>C(x)=x^{2}-4x+1000</md> Find the average rate of change in the total cost as <m>x</m> changes from <m>x=10</m> to <m>x=15</m>.
            </p>
          </statement>
          <answer>
              <p>$21 per unit</p>
          </answer>
        </exercise>

        <exercise xml:id="PRECALC-NWeqFrNZUw-parts" original="PRECALC/modules/m49455/index.cnxml" license="CC-BY-4.0">
        <statement>
          <ol marker="(a)" cols="2">
            <li>What is the difference between the average rate of change of a function on the interval <m>[x,x+h]</m> and the derivative of the function at <m>x?</m>
            </li>
            <li>A car traveled 110 miles during the time period from 2:00 <em>P.M.</em> to 4:00 <em>P.M.</em> What was the car's average velocity? At exactly 2:30 <em>P.M.</em>, the speed of the car registered exactly 62 miles per hour. What is another name for the speed of the car at 2:30 <em>P.M.</em>? Why does this speed differ from the average velocity?</li>
            <li>Explain the concept of the slope of a curve at point <m>x.</m>
            </li>
            <li>Suppose water is flowing into a tank at an average rate of 45 gallons per minute. Translate this statement into the language of mathematics.</li>
          </ol>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <ol marker="(a)" cols="2">
            <li/>
            <li>Average velocity is 55 miles per hour. The instantaneous velocity at 2:30 <em>p.m.</em> is 62 miles per hour. The instantaneous velocity measures the velocity of the car at an instant of time whereas the average velocity gives the velocity of the car over an interval.</li>
            <li/>
            <li>The average rate of change of the amount of water in the tank is 45 gallons per minute. If <m>f(x)</m> is the function giving the amount of water in the tank at any time <m>t,</m> then the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> between <m>t=a</m> and <m>t=b</m> is <m>f(a)+45(b-a).</m>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </answer>
      </exercise>
    </exercises>

